  "configuration_id": "config_027",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_012, acc=0.7250) uses scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted in multimodal multiprofile mode. All eight completed experiments strongly confirm that this combination of choices (scvi_n200 > scgpt/pca, multiprofile > singleprofile, transformer > avgpool, weighted ≥ concat, vit_l ≥ resnet50) is optimal. No untested multimodal multiprofile configuration with scvi_n200 offers a plausible path to exceed 0.725; the remaining untested scvi_n200 multimodal configs all involve a step-down (avgpool or resnet50). Question: This experiment tests RNA-only, singleprofile with scvi_n200 to establish a clean, minimal lower bound for the best RNA encoder in isolation, confirming the incremental value of the full multimodal multiprofile pipeline. Why this is the best use: With only 1 experiment remaining after this one, the primary goal shifts to minimizing total GPU cost while the best accuracy is already secured at 0.7250. config_027 requires no image processing, no multiprofile aggregation, and no fusion—making it the cheapest informative experiment (~0.2–0.3 GPU hours vs. 3–6 for multimodal multiprofile configs). It adds a useful reference point at negligible cost, keeping total GPU hours near 32.6 rather than adding 5+ hours for a multimodal run unlikely to improve on the current best."
}

